  era: "c. 2600\u20131900 BCE \xB7 Section 2 \xB7 Indus Valley Civilisation \xB7 c. 3300 \u2013 1300 BCE (mature phase c. 2600 \u2013 1900 BCE)"
  title: Harappan economy
  text: The economy rested on farming, herding, crafts and long-distance trade. Cities depended on surplus grain from villages, while specialised craftspeople produced beads, pottery, metalwork and shell objects for local use and export.
